# ==============================================================
# AVATR Admin Panel - Environment Variables
# ==============================================================
#
# For LOCAL development:
#   1. Copy this file to `.env.local`
#   2. Fill in your real values below
#   3. Restart `npm run dev`
#
# For PRODUCTION (Vercel):
#   Set these in Vercel Dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   Apply to: Production, Preview, Development (tick all 3)
#   Then re-deploy
#
# When these are set:
#   - The Setup page is skipped entirely (goes straight to Login)
#   - Support users cannot see or change Supabase credentials
#   - Admins won't see the "ตั้งค่าการเชื่อมต่อ" button either
#     (no need — credentials are managed via Vercel Dashboard)
#
# When these are NOT set (dev fallback):
#   - The app shows the Setup page and stores credentials in localStorage
#
# Where to find these values:
#   Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API
#   - Project URL  → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   - anon public  → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  (NOT service_role!)
#
# For Vercel API routes (server-side fallback for uploads/deletes):
#   - SUPABASE_URL
#   - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# ==============================================================

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
